message: "If you use WildTrace or its data, please cite it as below. Data CC BY 4.0, code MIT."
title: "WildTrace: the open atlas of illegal wildlife trade"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Verma
    given-names: Tarun
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tarunv13/wildtrace"
url: "https://tarunv13.github.io/wildtrace/"
license: MIT
# doi: filled in after Zenodo mints one for the first GitHub release
keywords:
  - illegal wildlife trade
  - wildlife trafficking
  - OSINT
  - CITES
  - link analysis
  - conservation
abstract: >-
  An open-source map of the global illegal wildlife trade in fauna and flora.
  A Python pipeline collects public reports (official government, enforcement
  and judicial releases first, then news), screens and extracts seizures,
  arrests and convictions, merges reports into cases, grades each case as
  validated, official, corroborated or single-report, and publishes a static
  atlas with an in-browser link-analysis workbench. No person accused is named.
